// EXAMPLE ONLY -- not wired into any build. Mixed board: two isx031 "simple yuv"
// GMSL cameras plus an ar0233 GMSL camera (all self discoverable -- ar0233 outputs
// YUV via its max9x deserializer just like isx031, despite the "GMSL Sensor" name
// suggesting Bayer), alongside an ov13b10 true Bayer camera (needs ISP demosaic/3A
// tuning, so it keeps its hand-authored sensors/ov13b10-uf.json). Every entry in
// "availableSensors" is still required (see getAvailableSensors(), which confirms
// each one is actually present via the live media graph); listing a sensor name in
// "autoDiscoverSensors" additionally selects it to be self discovered instead of
// loaded from "sensors/<name>.json" -- CameraParserInvoker builds its CameraInfo
// purely from SensorNodeDiscovery, deriving the sensor's own subdev entity name
// ("<sensor name> <I2CBus>", e.g. "isx031 a-0" for "isx031-a-0") from the resolved
// CSI port/I2C bus the same way a hand-authored "$I2CBUS" placeholder would (see
// CameraSensorsParser::runAutoDiscovery). Once a sensor is listed here its
// "sensors/<name>.json" file is never opened at all -- it can be deleted entirely
// (no need to even keep a stub with "discoverSensorEntity" in it, since
// runAutoDiscovery derives the subdev entity name internally). Sensors not listed
// in "autoDiscoverSensors" -- "ov13b10-uf" here -- fall back to loading
// "sensors/<name>.json" exactly as before, so Bayer/RAW sensors needing ISP/PSys/3A
// tuning can coexist on the same board as self-discovered ones. Self discovery still
// requires each listed sensor's graph to have already been linked/routed out-of-band
// (udev/board-init service, or kernel default routing) before ipu7-camera-hal starts,
// and its active output format to be a self-discoverable "simple yuv" passthrough one
// (see CameraUtils::getPixelFormatFromMBusCode).
//
{
    "Common" : {
        "version": 1.0,
        "platform": "IPU7",
        //  Self discover isx031-1, isx031-a and ar0233-1 (all YUV passthrough); no
        //  sensors/isx031-1.json, sensors/isx031-a.json or sensors/ar0233-1.json
        //  files are needed for these. ov13b10-uf keeps its hand-authored
        //  sensors/ov13b10-uf.json since it is a true Bayer/RAW sensor (SGRBG10,
        //  enableAIQ: true) needing ISP demosaic/3A tuning.
        "autoDiscoverSensors": ["isx031-1", "isx031-a", "ar0233-1"],
        //  The value format of availableSensors is "sensor name"-wf/uf-"CSI port ID".
        //  wf is world facing, and uf is user facing.
        "availableSensors": ["isx031-1-0", "isx031-a-0", "ar0233-1-3", "ov13b10-uf-2"],
        "videoStreamNum" : 2
    }
}
